  "failure_resolution_notes": [
    "The original core dependency rejected lowercase canonical digest-function spellings emitted by request.rs. The opaque followup core patch fixes that defect.",
    "Feature validation initially changed the plain-base split-storage contract. The final guard limits staged replay to feature-bearing context while keeping the base storage-suite path.",
    "The v2 nine-mutant run killed every mutant but restored only 26/28 format tests: a 50ms quorum RPC deadline expired under load and cold recovery raced a remaining storage clone after Raft core shutdown. The final fixture uses a 500ms RPC deadline and waits for each journal to become exclusively openable.",
    "The first explicit closed-journal wait revealed an intentional test-owned clone retained to final shutdown; the stale-leader test now drops it before teardown. That failed attempt is retained.",
    "Earlier exploratory logs and prior source hashes describe those earlier candidates; only current source hashes identify the final qualification."
  ],
